{"id":"5998e080b5d378a0","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md","title":"Self-Adjoint Operator","display":"df-self-adjoint — Self-Adjoint Operator","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-self-adjoint","aliases":["58-df-self-adjoint"],"display":"df-self-adjoint — Self-Adjoint Operator","depends_on":["[[58-df-hilbert-space]]","[[58-df-adjoint]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-self-adjoint"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-self-adjoint</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-self-adjoint — Self-Adjoint Operator"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"200eacd293b1282b\" href=\"?note=200eacd293b1282b\" title=\"58-df-adjoint\">58-df-adjoint</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T:H\\to H\">\\(T:H\\to H\\)</span> (bounded operator)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T^*:H\\to H\">\\(T^*:H\\to H\\)</span> (candidate adjoint operator)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H\">\\(H\\)</span> (Hilbert space, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"b70ce791d5b1a19b\" href=\"?note=b70ce791d5b1a19b\" title=\"58-df-hilbert-space\">58-df-hilbert-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\">\\(\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,H,H)\">\\(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,H,H)\\)</span> (bounded-operator adjoint relation, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"200eacd293b1282b\" href=\"?note=200eacd293b1282b\" title=\"58-df-adjoint\">58-df-adjoint</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint} \\vdash \\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,H)\\leftrightarrow\\exists T^*\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,H,H)\\land T=T^*\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint} \\vdash \\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,H)\\leftrightarrow\\exists T^*\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,H,H)\\land T=T^*\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom follows the upstream adjoint relation and therefore defines bounded self-adjoint operators. Unbounded self-adjointness requires equality of a densely defined operator and its unbounded adjoint, including equality of domains.</li>\n<li>They model observables in quantum mechanics.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-hilbert-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-adjoint","status":"resolved","id":"200eacd293b1282b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-adjoint]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-hilbert-space","status":"resolved","id":"b70ce791d5b1a19b","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$H$ (Hilbert space, see [[58-df-hilbert-space]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-adjoint","status":"resolved","id":"200eacd293b1282b","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,H,H)$ (bounded-operator adjoint relation, see [[58-df-adjoint]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T:H\\to H","display":false},{"tex":"T^*:H\\to H","display":false},{"tex":"H","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,H,H)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint} \\vdash \\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,H)\\leftrightarrow\\exists T^*\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,H,H)\\land T=T^*\\right)","display":true}],"bytes":1079,"backlinks":[{"id":"6408ad949910b0f7","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"8cd200016e351244","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"2ec0511903e19292","anchor":"ref-6","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$T$ (self-adjoint operator on $H$, see [[58-df-self-adjoint]])"},{"id":"93a99642b1c854e4","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S$ (bounded self-adjoint-operator predicate, see [[../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md]])"},{"id":"e052306286085efd","anchor":"ref-1","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1127","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-self-adjoint.md|58-df-self-adjoint]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["b70ce791d5b1a19b","200eacd293b1282b"]}